      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks. I also want to make sure they understand why this is such a controversial topic. Could you add a section that explains the main arguments used against substantive due process?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The controversy around substantive due process often centers on the idea of \"judicial activism,\" where critics argue that judges are making policy rather than just interpreting the law. Opponents contend that this allows unelected judges to create new rights that the people or elected legislatures have not approved. Furthermore, some legal thought points out that the concept can be too vague and lead to inconsistent and unpredictable legal outcomes across different cases.",
      "source": "target",
